    "title": "Refresh the work guide to current GitHub status",
    "body": "## Summary\n\nRefresh the cross-project work guide to current GitHub state before public publication.\n\n- **Snapshot.** Backlog read at 2026-09-24 09:15 UTC: 94 open issues (Hub 60, Nanoleaf 19, Pixoo 15). Merged-work history read at 09:07 UTC from Hub `fcb6b21`, Nanoleaf `08b6b83` and Pixoo `01da65d`.\n- **Coverage.** Removes 13 issues that closed since the last edition (Hub #21, #152, #154, #155, #175, #191, #195, #220; Nanoleaf #15, #46, #75, #76, #77). Assigns the 13 new open issues a primary guide: Hub #222, #227, #229, #231, #232, #233; Nanoleaf #90, #91, #92, #100, #108; Pixoo #76, #77.\n- **Stale prose.** Rewrites the topic next steps, Useful next steps, decisions, device tracks and reading notes that still described closed work as pending. Adds archive rows for delivered read state, session expiry, legacy hook removal, the Lines + Panels trial, Tidbyt acceptance, installed general controls, hub MCP media tools, shared playback and the overview refresh.\n- **Architecture.** The Nanoleaf runtime view (A3) takes the installed evidence from Nanoleaf #46 and #89 without moving its pins. The section intro notes what A2 does not draw yet (Hub #21, #18, #175). The atlas-embedded A2 and S4 renders are byte-identical, so the atlas is unchanged. The Music preset boundary now cites Hub #175 instead of #36.\n- **Timeline fixes.** Found while checking this edition: overlapping history axis labels and milestone captions, roadmap labels overflowing their nodes, and several roadmap nodes stacked on one column, which hid open Hub #73. Adds layout asserts so these fail the build.\n- **Checks.** Swaps browser and maintenance-test examples that pointed at issues now closed (Hub #21, #195; Nanoleaf #15, #46). The offline-badge check now reads its expected status from the built snapshot.\n- **Cleanup.** Removes `docs/work-guide/updates.md`. #169 retired it, #190 re-added it by mistake, and its only entry is already in the milestone archive.\n\nTracker changes made alongside this refresh: removed stale `blocked` labels, each with a comment, where every recorded blocker is closed (Hub #20, #36, #37, #38, #39, #51, #52, #218, #229; Nanoleaf #17). Also removed leftover workflow labels from closed issues (Hub #10, #15, #86, #197, #200; Nanoleaf #31; Pixoo #38, #47), as docs/sdlc.md requires.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `python3 docs/work-guide/work/build_guide.py` passed. Rebuilding after commit produced no output drift. Guide SHA-256: `504878b7b4c2bb3cb4f99ebccbf2d7fc6140507a721cb57562fdbdb633a275b4`.\n- `python3 docs/work-guide/work/test_maintenance.py` passed (12 tests).\n- `node docs/work-guide/work/check_guide.cjs` passed (Node 24.21.0, Playwright 1.63.0, Chromium 1243). It covers navigation, search, task briefs, live and offline status, the timeline, diagrams and print restoration at desktop and phone widths.\n- `ARCHIFY_DIR=~/.agents/skills/archify python3 docs/work-guide/work/architecture_diagrams.py`: all nine diagrams 9/9 with no errors or warnings. Only `arch-nanoleaf-linux` changed.\n- `git diff --check` passed. All 28 changed paths are under `docs/work-guide/`.\n- Screenshots, the print PDF and the verification receipt are kept outside Git in the main checkout at `.local/evidence/guide-publish-20260924/`.\n\nThis is a dated snapshot. It installs nothing and operates no devices. The public publication PR follows this Hub PR after reviews, merge and the guide-only CI receipt.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
